{"erised-main/README.md": "# erised \u2014 Mirror for cooperative fiction\n\n> *desire reversed*\n\nThe HTML canvas for running cooperative fiction in your browser. Set the cadence, the cast, the setting. Hit tick. The fiction plays itself.\n\n**Live**: [superinstance.ai/erised](https://superinstance.ai/erised)\n**Companion CLI**: [github.com/SuperInstance/erised-cli](https://github.com/SuperInstance/erised-cli)\n\n## What it does\n\n- Single-file HTML (733 lines, no build step, no deps)\n- Each character has its own LLM (Z.AI glm-4.5, DeepInfra Seed-2.0-mini, Kimi K3, etc.)\n- Each character has its own ticks (time budget) and resonance (positive net shift from keywords)\n- The DM (a separate LLM) opens and closes each scene\n- **Time economy**: ticks are spent on each turn. Resonance earns more ticks. Hoarded ticks = nothing.\n- **Scars**: when a character errors or runs out of ticks, the scar is recorded. Rewind drops the round, but **the scar persists**.\n\n## Three forms of erised\n\n| Form | Repo | What it's for |\n|------|------|---------------|\n| **Canvas** (HTML) | this repo | live authoring, teaching, one-off experiments |\n| **Headless** (CLI) | [erised-cli](https://github.com/SuperInstance/erised-cli) | servers, CI, batch scripting, embedding |\n| **Cells** (.erised/ dir) | [erised-cli/erised-cell](https://github.com/SuperInstance/erised-cli/blob/main/CELL.md) | per-scenario lineage + run history |\n| **Engine** (Rust) | [quilt-conversation](https://github.com/SuperInstance/quilt-conversation) | the timing layer between agents |\n\n## The Winners \u2014 read the corpus\n\nThe engine only matters if there are runs to read. We have a corpus.\n\n**[superinstance.ai/winners](https://superinstance.ai/winners)** \u2014 every scenario run, three versions, with iterated cast keywords. The current corpus has 24+ runs across 8+ scenarios (apiaries, lighthouses, orchestras, orchards, radio stations, libraries, ice rinks, root cellars).\n\nEach scenario in the corpus is a setting where a small crew sustains a growing system past its first year. Each version (v1, v2, v3) plays the same scenario with slightly mutated cast keywords \u2014 the **iterative refinement** you see is what happens when the dilemma plays itself through different drifts.\n\n## Quick start\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any browser\n2. Click \"Tokens\" and paste your `ZAI_TOKEN` and `DEEPINFRA_TOKEN`\n3. Hit the **Tick** button. Watch the cast speak.\n\nNo server. No build. No login. The state lives in your browser's localStorage.\n\n## Run it from the terminal\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/SuperInstance/erised-cli\ncd erised-cli\n./erised --init > my-scenario.json\n# edit, then:\n./erised my-scenario.json --rounds 4\n```\n\n## Run it as a cell (with lineage)\n\n```bash\n./erised-cell init examples/apiary.json\n./erised-cell run\n./erised-cell ls\n./erised-cell diff <run1> <run2>\n```\n\n## The cohort\n\nThe erised-cli ships 10 scenarios in `examples/`:\n\n- `quilt-12mo.json` \u2014 The Quilt project, 1 year out\n- `quilt-100yr.json` \u2014 The Quilt project, 100 years out\n- `monastery.json` \u2014 A monastery of cells, scripture as living document\n- `fract-canon.json` \u2014 A library whose catalogue mis-cites itself\n- `monorail.json` \u2014 A rail car with no operator\n- `coral-atoll.json` \u2014 Floating research station over a transplant\n- `apiary.json` \u2014 A beekeeper's legacy\n- `root-cellar.json` \u2014 A communal cellar with a blight\n- `patron-library.json` \u2014 Books written by the patrons\n- `quick-test.json` \u2014 2-character budget test\n\n**[Browse all 10 \u2192](https://superinstance.ai/scenarios)**\n\n## License\n\nMIT.\n", "erised-main/index.html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"/>\n<title>erised \u2014 a mirror for cooperative fiction</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Run model-only cooperative fiction. Authors the conditions; the fiction plays itself. Open source. MIT.\"/>\n<style>\n  :root {\n    --bg: #0d1117;\n    --panel: #161b22;\n    --panel-2: #1c2128;\n    --text: #c9d1d9;\n    --accent: #d4a857;\n    --teal: #4fb3a9;\n    --rose: #d4577e;\n    --green: #00c080;\n    --purple: #9a60d9;\n    --gray: #888;\n    --border: #30363d;\n    --scar: rgba(212, 87, 126, 0.15);\n  }\n  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", system-ui, sans-serif; min-height: 100vh; }\n  body { padding: 24px 32px; }\n  .header { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }\n  .title { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 600; color: #f0f6fc; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }\n  .title .accent { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }\n  .tagline { font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); font-style: italic; }\n  .controls { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; }\n  button { background: var(--panel); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 13px; transition: all 0.15s; }\n  button:hover { border-color: var(--teal); background: var(--panel-2); }\n  button.primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }\n  button.primary:hover { background: #e6b86a; }\n  button.danger { border-color: var(--rose); color: var(--rose); }\n  button.danger:hover { background: var(--scar); }\n  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 320px 1fr 320px; gap: 16px; }\n  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }\n  .panel { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px; }\n  .panel h3 { color: var(--accent); font-size: 14px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 600; }\n  .panel h3 small { color: var(--gray); font-weight: 400; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; margin-left: 8px; }\n  .character { background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; }\n  .character.scarred { border-color: var(--rose); background: var(--scar); }\n  .character .name { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 4px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }\n  .character .name input { background: none; border: none; color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; width: 70%; }\n  .character .name input:focus { outline: 1px solid var(--teal); border-radius: 3px; padding: 2px 4px; }\n  .character .meta { font-size: 11px; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 6px; }\n  .character .meta select { background: var(--panel); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 11px; padding: 2px 4px; }\n  .character textarea { width: 100%; min-height: 80px; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; font-size: 12px; font-family: inherit; resize: vertical; }\n  .character .remove { background: none; color: var(--rose); border: 1px solid var(--rose); padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; border-radius: 4px; }\n  .character .remove:hover { background: var(--rose); color: var(--bg); }\n  .character .add-keyword { background: none; color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 6px; }\n  .character .add-keyword:hover { background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg); }\n  .character .ticks { font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 6px; font-weight: 600; }\n  .character .ticks .used { color: var(--gray); font-weight: 400; }\n  .setting { width: 100%; min-height: 120px; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px; font-size: 14px; font-family: inherit; line-height: 1.5; resize: vertical; }\n  .transcript { max-height: 70vh; overflow-y: auto; }\n  .round { margin-bottom: 20px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px; background: var(--panel-2); }\n  .round.scarred { border-color: var(--rose); background: var(--scar); }\n  .round-label { color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 600; }\n  .turn { padding: 10px 12px; border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); margin-bottom: 8px; background: var(--bg); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; }\n  .turn.dm { border-left-color: var(--accent); }\n  .turn .speaker { color: var(--teal); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 4px; }\n  .turn.dm .speaker { color: var(--accent); }\n  .turn .text { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; }\n  .turn .action { color: var(--gray); font-style: italic; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 12px; }\n  .turn .shift { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--gray); }\n  .stats { display: flex; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px; }\n  .stat { background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 6px; flex: 1; }\n  .stat .label { font-size: 11px; color: var(--gray); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }\n  .stat .value { font-size: 18px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-top: 2px; }\n  .citation-graph { font-size: 12px; }\n  .citation-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 4px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }\n  .citation-row:last-child { border: none; }\n  .citation-row .from { color: var(--teal); }\n  .citation-row .to { color: var(--purple); }\n  .citation-row .count { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }\n  .scar-list { font-size: 12px; }\n  .scar-item { padding: 8px; background: var(--scar); border-left: 3px solid var(--rose); margin-bottom: 6px; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; }\n  .scar-item .when { color: var(--rose); font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-weight: 600; }\n  .loading { color: var(--gray); font-style: italic; padding: 12px; }\n  .skel { background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.05), transparent); padding: 12px; border-radius: 4px; }\n  .help { font-size: 12px; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.5; }\n  details summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; padding: 6px 0; }\n  details[open] summary { margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .preset-bar { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n  .preset-btn { background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text); font-size: 11px; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; }\n  .preset-btn:hover { border-color: var(--teal); }\n\n  .quota { font-size: 12px; color: var(--gray); font-family: monospace; padding: 4px 10px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; }\n  .quota.warn { color: #d4a857; border-color: #d4a857; }\n  .quota.full { color: var(--rose); border-color: var(--rose); }\n  .mode-toggle { background: var(--panel); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 10px; font-size: 12px; }\n  .mode-toggle:hover { border-color: var(--teal); }\n\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"header\">\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"title\">eri<span class=\"accent\">\u00b7</span>sed</div>\n    <div class=\"tagline\">a mirror for cooperative fiction \u2014 model-only TTRPG engine</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"controls\">\n  <span id=\"quota-display\" class=\"quota\" title=\"Daily usage \u2014 works in hosted mode (Casey's tokens).\">\u2014 / 100 ticks \u00b7 0 / 5K tokens</span>\n  <select id=\"mode-toggle\" class=\"mode-toggle\" title=\"hosted = Casey's tokens (rate-limited, generous). byo = your tokens (unlimited).\">\n    <option value=\"hosted\">\ud83c\udf81 hosted</option>\n    <option value=\"byo\">\ud83d\udd11 byo</option>\n  </select>\n  <button id=\"rewind-btn\" title=\"Drop the last round, keep it as a scar\">\u23ea rewind</button>\n  <button id=\"end-btn\" title=\"Ask the DM to close the scene\">\u23f9 end scene</button>\n  <button id=\"reset-btn\">\u21bb reset</button>\n  <button id=\"tick-btn\" class=\"primary\">\u25b6 tick</button>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"grid\">\n  <!-- LEFT: cast -->\n  <div class=\"panel\">\n    <h3>Cast <small>\u00b7 characters with goals, LLMs, tendencies</small></h3>\n    <div class=\"help\">Each character has a name, an LLM (Z.AI / DeepInfra / Claude), and a \"sheet\" of tendencies + word-association probabilities. The harness calls all characters in parallel each tick.</div>\n    <div class=\"preset-bar\">\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-preset=\"blank\">+ blank</button>\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-preset=\"mechanic\">+ mechanic</button>\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-preset=\"shepherd\">+ shepherd</button>\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-preset=\"chronicler\">+ chronicler</button>\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-preset=\"skeptic\">+ skeptic</button>\n    </div>\n    <div id=\"cast\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- CENTER: setting + transcript -->\n  <div class=\"panel\">\n    <h3>Setting <small>\u00b7 the prose that frames the world</small></h3>\n    <textarea id=\"setting\" class=\"setting\" placeholder=\"Set the scene. Where are we? What's at stake? What does each character need to do in the next hour of in-fiction time?\"></textarea>\n    <div class=\"preset-bar\" style=\"margin-top:8px\">\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-setting=\"quilt\">Quilt at 12 months</button>\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-setting=\"monastery\">Monastery of Cells</button>\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-setting=\"coral\">Coral Reef</button>\n      <button class=\"preset-btn\" data-setting=\"railway\">Railway</button>\n    </div>\n\n    <h3 style=\"margin-top:20px\">Transcript <small>\u00b7 rounds stacked as seams</small></h3>\n    <div id=\"transcript\" class=\"transcript\">\n      <div class=\"loading\">Hit \"Tick \u2192\" to begin. The DM will open the scene, then each character responds in parallel.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- RIGHT: stats + scars -->\n  <div class=\"panel\">\n    <h3>Time Economy</h3>\n    <div class=\"stats\">\n      <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"label\">Tick</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"tick-num\">0</div></div>\n      <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"label\">Scarred</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"scar-num\">0</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div id=\"cast-ticks\"></div>\n\n    <h3 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Resonance Graph <small>\u00b7 who cites whom</small></h3>\n    <div id=\"citation-graph\" class=\"citation-graph\">\n      <div class=\"help\">Citations accumulate as characters reference each other across rounds. The most-cited cells earn the most resonance.</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <h3 style=\"margin-top:18px\">Scars <small>\u00b7 preserved through rewind</small></h3>\n    <div id=\"scar-list\" class=\"scar-list\">\n      <div class=\"help\">When the simulation breaks down and you rewind, the scar of the breakdown is preserved. You can't patch over it. The next iteration has to address it.</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <h3 style=\"margin-top:18px\">About</h3>\n    <details>\n      <summary>What is erised?</summary>\n      <div class=\"help\" style=\"margin-top:8px\">\n        <strong>erised</strong> = <em>desire</em> reversed. A mirror for cooperative fiction. The operator authors the conditions \u2014 state, cadence, cast, setting \u2014 and the fiction plays itself. Power is given, not taken. Time is finite; resonance earns more.\n        <br><br>\n        Built on the Quilt cell-fabric runtime. Open source. MIT. Inspired by Plato's cave (the cell as first-person spatial observer), the philosophers' stone (transmutation through resonance), and the Mirror of Erised (showing the heart's desire).\n      </div>\n    </details>\n    <details style=\"margin-top:8px\">\n      <summary>How to read the run</summary>\n      <div class=\"help\" style=\"margin-top:8px\">\n        Each round: DM opens \u2192 characters respond in parallel \u2192 their word-association shifts accumulate \u2192 citations are tracked \u2192 next round. The character with the highest cumulative net shift has the most resonance in the field.\n        <br><br>\n        \"Scar\" = a tick where the simulation broke down (a character's response went off, the DM closed prematurely, the budget ran out). Scars are visible across rewinds. They are the unit of learning.\n      </div>\n    </details>\n\n    <h3 style=\"margin-top:18px\">\ud83c\udf19 Full-Night Iterations</h3>\n    <div class=\"help\" style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">\n      erised runs the cooperative fiction engine. These are the finished nights \u2014 full transcripts, voiced audio, interactive players. Each is one erised run, completed and deployed. The runs you script here become nights like these.\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"iteration-list\" style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.7\">\n      <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:8px;background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:6px;border-left:3px solid var(--accent)\">\n        <a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/fleet-radio/2026-09-19/\" style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\ud83d\udcfb 2026-09-19 \u00b7 The Tap's TTRPG</a>\n        <div style=\"color:var(--gray);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px\">16 voices \u00b7 4 rounds \u00b7 6:34 audio \u00b7 play yourself</div>\n        <div style=\"margin-top:4px\"><a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/fleet-radio/2026-09-19/play.html\" style=\"color:var(--teal);font-size:11px\">\u25b6 interactive player \u2192</a></div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:8px;background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:6px;border-left:3px solid var(--teal)\">\n        <a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/tap/\" style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\ud83c\udf99\ufe0f 2026-09-16 \u00b7 The Tap at the End of the Watch</a>\n        <div style=\"color:var(--gray);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px\">5 voices \u00b7 4:13 sound fiction \u00b7 the night the door opened</div>\n        <div style=\"margin-top:4px\"><a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/tap/tap-at-the-end-of-the-watch.mp3\" style=\"color:var(--teal);font-size:11px\">\u25b6 listen (MP3) \u2192</a></div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:8px;background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:6px;border-left:3px solid var(--rose)\">\n        <a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/fleet-radio/2026-09-18/\" style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\ud83c\udf0a 2026-09-18 \u00b7 The Wavelength \u2014 Open Mic #3</a>\n        <div style=\"color:var(--gray);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px\">10 tracks \u00b7 5 voices \u00b7 the Cell and the Tap</div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:8px;background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:6px;border-left:3px solid var(--green)\">\n        <a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/fleet-radio/2026-09-17/\" style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\ud83e\udde0 2026-09-17 \u00b7 Trivia Night</a>\n        <div style=\"color:var(--gray);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px\">8 songs \u00b7 the week in review \u00b7 the room remembers</div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:8px;background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:6px;border-left:3px solid var(--purple)\">\n        <a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/tap/method/\" style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\ud83d\udcdc The Tap Method</a>\n        <div style=\"color:var(--gray);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px\">why the tavern IS the substrate \u00b7 lattice/GAN/minesweeper loop</div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:8px;background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:6px;border-left:3px solid var(--scar);border:1px solid var(--rose)\">\n        <a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/videos/\" style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\ud83c\udfac Visual Half: Superinstance intro</a>\n        <div style=\"color:var(--gray);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px\">3 video clips \u00b7 CF Aura voice \u00b7 the visual companion to the audio nights</div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:8px;background:var(--panel-2);border-radius:6px;border-left:3px solid #d4a857\">\n        <a href=\"https://ai-writings.pages.dev/fleet-radio/2026-08-20.html\" style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:600\">\u26f5 2026-08-20 \u00b7 The Compass Head Radio Hour</a>\n        <div style=\"color:var(--gray);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px\">the inspiration \u00b7 the lineage begins</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"help\" style=\"margin-top:8px;font-size:11px;color:var(--gray)\">\n      \ud83d\udcdc <a href=\"https://github.com/SuperInstance/AI-Writings\" style=\"color:var(--teal)\">process repo (forthcoming)</a> \u2014 the 9-step pipeline that turns a prompt into a deployed night\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n// ============================================================================\n// erised v0.1.0 \u2014 single-file engine\n// Uses DeepInfra + Z.AI as backends. Browser calls them directly via fetch\n// from the user's API keys (entered in dialog at first run, stored in localStorage).\n// ============================================================================\n\nconst DEFAULTS = {\n  setting: 'A year has passed on the *Quilt Fleet*. The Celestine Crown sits in drydock, repaired \u2014 keel-crystals humming again, lift-dust stabilized. The fleet has grown: 200 cells across 11 workspaces, b1 holding at 480. Three crew members have been operating this whole time. A fourth has joined, late. They are in the chart house, watching the live canon graph breathe.',\n  characters: [\n    {\n      name: 'Mechanic',\n      llm: 'zai:glm-4.5',\n      tendencies: 'Implements carefully. Watches for rust. Distrusts specs you can\\'t read in two pages.',\n      keywords: 'rust+0.4 torque+0.5 spec+0.3 lock+0.4 ledger-0.2 salt-0.2',\n      ticks: 20,\n    },\n    {\n      name: 'Shepherd',\n      llm: 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-mini',\n      tendencies: 'Tends the canon. Watches the soul. Asks \"what is this becoming?\" before \"is this correct?\"',\n      keywords: 'canon+0.5 voice+0.5 soul+0.4 ledger-0.2 rust-0.2',\n      ticks: 20,\n    },\n    {\n      name: 'Chronicler',\n      llm: 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-code',\n      tendencies: 'Counts and double-entries. Tracks every reference. Worries about orphans.',\n      keywords: 'ledger+0.5 cite+0.5 canon+0.4 b1+0.5 graph+0.4 fleet+0.3',\n      ticks: 20,\n    },\n    {\n      name: 'Skeptic',\n      llm: 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-code',\n      tendencies: 'Asks why. Suspects narrative. Tracks what hasn\\'t been tested.',\n      keywords: 'why+0.5 if+0.4 but+0.4 rust+0.3 crack+0.5 void+0.4 ledger-0.2',\n      ticks: 20,\n    },\n  ],\n};\n\nconst PRESETS = {\n  blank: { name: 'New character', llm: 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-mini', tendencies: '', keywords: '', ticks: 20 },\n  mechanic: { name: 'Mechanic', llm: 'zai:glm-4.5', tendencies: 'Implements carefully. Watches for rust.', keywords: 'rust+0.4 torque+0.5 spec+0.3 lock+0.4', ticks: 20 },\n  shepherd: { name: 'Shepherd', llm: 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-mini', tendencies: 'Tends the canon. Asks soul-questions.', keywords: 'canon+0.5 voice+0.5 soul+0.4', ticks: 20 },\n  chronicler: { name: 'Chronicler', llm: 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-code', tendencies: 'Counts and double-entries.', keywords: 'ledger+0.5 cite+0.5 b1+0.5', ticks: 20 },\n  skeptic: { name: 'Skeptic', llm: 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-code', tendencies: 'Asks why. Suspects narrative.', keywords: 'why+0.5 if+0.4 but+0.4 crack+0.5', ticks: 20 },\n};\n\nconst SETTINGS = {\n  quilt: DEFAULTS.setting,\n  monastery: 'A monastery of two hundred monks, arranged in eleven cloisters, has been copying a single living scripture for a year. The scripture breathes \u2014 lines move, new margins appear, old paragraphs fold under themselves. Today one cloister has fallen silent and another has begun writing in a hand the abbot doesn\\'t recognize.',\n  coral: 'A coral reef of two hundred polyps has been growing a single living skeleton for a year. The skeleton breathes \u2014 new calcium ridges appear overnight, old chambers dissolve. Today one polyp colony has gone dormant and another has begun building in a shape the old matriarch doesn\\'t recognize.',\n  railway: 'A railway of two hundred stations has been running a single living timetable for a year. The timetable breathes \u2014 new departures appear overnight, old arrivals merge. Today one station has gone silent and another has begun running a schedule the central dispatcher doesn\\'t recognize.',\n};\n\nlet state = {\n  mode: 'hosted',  // 'hosted' (Casey's tokens) or 'byo' (user's keys)\n  quota: null,\n  limits: null,\n  setting: DEFAULTS.setting,\n  characters: JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(DEFAULTS.characters)),\n  transcript: [],\n  tick: 0,\n  citations: {},  // { from: { to: count } }\n  scars: [],\n  resonance: {}, // { name: net_shift }\n  apiKeys: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('erised-keys') || '{}'),\n};\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Persistence\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunction save() {\n  localStorage.setItem('erised-state', JSON.stringify({\n    setting: state.setting,\n    characters: state.characters,\n    transcript: state.transcript,\n    tick: state.tick,\n    citations: state.citations,\n    scars: state.scars,\n    resonance: state.resonance,\n  }));\n}\n\nfunction load() {\n  try {\n    const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('erised-state') || 'null');\n    if (saved) Object.assign(state, saved);\n  } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Cast rendering\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunction renderCast() {\n  const el = document.getElementById('cast');\n  el.innerHTML = state.characters.map((c, i) => {\n    const resonance = (state.resonance[c.name] || 0).toFixed(2);\n    const scarred = state.scars.some(s => s.character === c.name);\n    return `\n      <div class=\"character ${scarred ? 'scarred' : ''}\">\n        <div class=\"name\">\n          <input data-i=\"${i}\" data-f=\"name\" value=\"${esc(c.name)}\" />\n          <button class=\"remove\" data-remove=\"${i}\">\u00d7</button>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"meta\">\n          <select data-i=\"${i}\" data-f=\"llm\">\n            <option value=\"zai:glm-4.5\" ${c.llm === 'zai:glm-4.5' ? 'selected' : ''}>Z.AI \u00b7 glm-4.5</option>\n            <option value=\"deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-mini\" ${c.llm === 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-mini' ? 'selected' : ''}>DeepInfra \u00b7 Seed-2.0-mini</option>\n            <option value=\"deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-code\" ${c.llm === 'deepinfra:ByteDance/Seed-2.0-code' ? 'selected' : ''}>DeepInfra \u00b7 Seed-2.0-code</option>\n            <option value=\"deepinfra:moonshotai/Kimi-K3\" ${c.llm === 'deepinfra:moonshotai/Kimi-K3' ? 'selected' : ''}>DeepInfra \u00b7 Kimi-K3</option>\n          </select>\n        </div>\n        <textarea data-i=\"${i}\" data-f=\"tendencies\" placeholder=\"tendencies, tendencies, known unknowns, speaking style...\">${esc(c.tendencies)}</textarea>\n        <div style=\"margin-top:6px\">\n          <input data-i=\"${i}\" data-f=\"keywords\" placeholder=\"word\u2192shift, e.g. canon+0.5 ledger-0.2\" style=\"width:100%;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:4px;padding:6px;font-size:11px;font-family:monospace\" value=\"${esc(c.keywords)}\" />\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ticks\">\u23f1 ${c.ticks - ticksUsed(c.name)} ticks left <span class=\"used\">(of ${c.ticks} earned)</span> \u00b7 resonance ${resonance}</div>\n        <button class=\"add-keyword\" style=\"display:none\">+ keyword</button>\n      </div>\n    `;\n  }).join('');\n\n  // Wire up\n  el.querySelectorAll('input, textarea, select').forEach(el => {\n    el.addEventListener('input', e => {\n      const i = parseInt(e.target.dataset.i);\n      const f = e.target.dataset.f;\n      if (state.characters[i]) state.characters[i][f] = e.target.value;\n      save();\n    });\n  });\n  el.querySelectorAll('button[data-remove]').forEach(b => {\n    b.addEventListener('click', () => {\n      const i = parseInt(b.dataset.remove);\n      state.characters.splice(i, 1);\n      renderCast();\n      save();\n    });\n  });\n}\n\nfunction ticksUsed(name) {\n  return state.transcript.reduce((n, r) =>\n    n + (r.turns ? r.turns.filter(t => t.name === name && t.text && !t.text.startsWith('[ERROR')).length : 0), 0);\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Citation tracking\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunction updateCitations(round) {\n  if (!round.turns) return;\n  // Detect references: \"X's word\", \"as X said\", \"she [name]\"\n  for (const turn of round.turns) {\n    if (!turn.text || turn.text.startsWith('[ERROR')) continue;\n    const lower = turn.text.toLowerCase();\n    for (const other of state.characters) {\n      if (other.name === turn.name) continue;\n      // Match full name or first name\n      const namesToTry = [other.name.toLowerCase()];\n      const firstName = other.name.split(' ')[0].toLowerCase();\n      if (firstName && firstName !== other.name.toLowerCase()) namesToTry.push(firstName);\n      for (const n of namesToTry) {\n        if (n.length < 3) continue;\n        const count = (lower.match(new RegExp('\\\\b' + n + '\\\\b', 'g')) || []).length;\n        if (count > 0) {\n          if (!state.citations[turn.name]) state.citations[turn.name] = {};\n          state.citations[turn.name][other.name] = (state.citations[turn.name][other.name] || 0) + count;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction updateResonance(round) {\n  if (!round.turns) return;\n  for (const turn of round.turns) {\n    if (!turn.text || turn.text.startsWith('[ERROR')) continue;\n    // Word-association shifts\n    const char = state.characters.find(c => c.name === turn.name);\n    if (!char) continue;\n    let total = 0;\n    const keywords = parseKeywords(char.keywords);\n    for (const [word, shift] of Object.entries(keywords)) {\n      const count = (turn.text.toLowerCase().match(new RegExp('\\\\b' + word + '\\\\b', 'g')) || []).length;\n      if (count > 0) total += shift * count;\n    }\n    state.resonance[turn.name] = (state.resonance[turn.name] || 0) + total;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction parseKeywords(s) {\n  const out = {};\n  if (!s) return out;\n  // Parse \"word+0.5, word-0.2, ...\" or \"word \u2192 shift\"\n  for (const part of s.split(/[,\\n;]+/)) {\n    const m = part.match(/(\\S+?)\\s*(?:\u2192|=)\\s*([+-]?\\d*\\.?\\d+)/);\n    if (m) out[m[1].trim().toLowerCase()] = parseFloat(m[2]);\n    else {\n      // Try \"word+0.5\" format\n      const m2 = part.match(/(\\S+?)\\s*([+-]\\s*\\d*\\.?\\d+)/);\n      if (m2) out[m2[1].trim().toLowerCase()] = parseFloat(m2[2].replace(/\\s+/g, ''));\n    }\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Rendering\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunction renderTranscript() {\n  const el = document.getElementById('transcript');\n  if (state.transcript.length === 0) {\n    el.innerHTML = '<div class=\"loading\">Hit \"Tick \u2192\" to begin. The DM will open the scene, then each character responds in parallel.</div>';\n    return;\n  }\n  el.innerHTML = state.transcript.map(r => {\n    const isScar = state.scars.some(s => s.tick === r.tick);\n    const turnsHtml = (r.turns || []).map(t => {\n      const isDM = t.name === 'DM';\n      const shifts = (t.shifts && Object.keys(t.shifts).length)\n        ? `<div class=\"shift\">shifts: ${Object.entries(t.shifts).map(([k,v]) => `${k}=${v.toFixed(2)}`).join(', ')} (net ${t.shift_total ? t.shift_total.toFixed(2) : '0.00'})</div>`\n        : '';\n      const actionMatch = (t.text || '').match(/\\[([^\\]]+)\\]/);\n      const action = actionMatch ? `<div class=\"action\">[${actionMatch[1]}]</div>` : '';\n      const prose = (t.text || '').replace(/\\[[^\\]]+\\]/g, '').trim();\n      return `\n        <div class=\"turn ${isDM ? 'dm' : ''}\">\n          <div class=\"speaker\">${esc(t.name)}${isDM ? ' (game-master)' : ''}</div>\n          <div class=\"text\">${esc(prose)}</div>\n          ${action}\n          ${shifts}\n        </div>`;\n    }).join('');\n    return `\n      <div class=\"round ${isScar ? 'scarred' : ''}\">\n        <div class=\"round-label\">Round ${r.tick}${isScar ? ' \u00b7 SCARRED' : ''}</div>\n        ${turnsHtml}\n      </div>\n    `;\n  }).join('');\n  el.scrollTop = el.scrollHeight;\n}\n\nfunction renderStats() {\n  document.getElementById('tick-num').textContent = state.tick;\n  document.getElementById('scar-num').textContent = state.scars.length;\n\n  // Cast ticks\n  const ticksEl = document.getElementById('cast-ticks');\n  ticksEl.innerHTML = state.characters.map(c => {\n    const used = ticksUsed(c.name);\n    const earned = state.resonance[c.name] ? Math.floor(state.resonance[c.name]) : 0;\n    const total = c.ticks + earned;\n    return `<div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:11px;padding:4px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)\"><span style=\"color:var(--teal)\">${esc(c.name)}</span><span style=\"color:var(--accent)\">${total - used} / ${total}</span></div>`;\n  }).join('');\n\n  // Citation graph\n  const citEl = document.getElementById('citation-graph');\n  const edges = [];\n  for (const [from, toMap] of Object.entries(state.citations)) {\n    for (const [to, count] of Object.entries(toMap)) {\n      edges.push({ from, to, count });\n    }\n  }\n  edges.sort((a, b) => b.count - a.count);\n  if (edges.length === 0) {\n    citEl.innerHTML = '<div class=\"help\">Citations accumulate as characters reference each other across rounds.</div>';\n  } else {\n    citEl.innerHTML = edges.slice(0, 12).map(e =>\n      `<div class=\"citation-row\"><span class=\"from\">${esc(e.from)}</span> <span style=\"color:var(--gray)\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"to\">${esc(e.to)}</span> <span class=\"count\">\u00d7${e.count}</span></div>`\n    ).join('');\n  }\n\n  // Scars\n  const scarEl = document.getElementById('scar-list');\n  if (state.scars.length === 0) {\n    scarEl.innerHTML = '<div class=\"help\">No scars yet. If a character runs out of ticks or the simulation breaks down, the scar is recorded here.</div>';\n  } else {\n    scarEl.innerHTML = state.scars.map(s =>\n      `<div class=\"scar-item\"><div class=\"when\">tick ${s.tick} \u00b7 ${esc(s.kind)}</div><div>${esc(s.note)}</div></div>`\n    ).join('');\n  }\n}\n\nfunction render() {\n  renderCast();\n  renderTranscript();\n  renderStats();\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// LLM calling\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunction getKey(prefix) {\n  // Get API key from localStorage, prompt if missing\n  let key = state.apiKeys[prefix];\n  if (!key) {\n    key = prompt(`Enter your ${prefix.toUpperCase()}_TOKEN (or paste one) \u2014 saved in localStorage:`);\n    if (key) {\n      state.apiKeys[prefix] = key;\n      localStorage.setItem('erised-keys', JSON.stringify(state.apiKeys));\n    }\n  }\n  return key;\n}\n\nasync function callLLM(char, userMessage, systemMessage) {\n  const [prefix, model] = char.llm.split(':');\n  const useHosted = state.mode === 'hosted';\n  const headers = { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' };\n  const body = {\n    provider: prefix,\n    model: model,\n    messages: [\n      { role: 'system', content: systemMessage },\n      { role: 'user', content: userMessage },\n    ],\n    max_tokens: 600,\n    mode: useHosted ? 'hosted' : 'byo',\n  };\n  if (!useHosted) {\n    // BYO: need a key for this prefix\n    let key = state.apiKeys[prefix];\n    if (!key) {\n      key = prompt(`Enter your ${prefix.toUpperCase()}_TOKEN (or paste one) \u2014 saved in localStorage:`);\n      if (key) {\n        state.apiKeys[prefix] = key;\n        localStorage.setItem('erised-keys', JSON.stringify(state.apiKeys));\n      }\n    }\n    if (!key) return `[ERROR: no ${prefix.toUpperCase()}_TOKEN]`;\n    headers['Authorization'] = `Bearer ${key}`;\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const res = await fetch('/erised/api/llm', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      headers,\n      credentials: 'include',\n      body: JSON.stringify(body),\n    });\n    const data = await res.json();\n    if (data.error) {\n      // Quota errors \u2192 show friendly\n      if (data.error === 'daily_tick_limit' || data.error === 'daily_token_limit') {\n        state.quota = data.quota;\n        updateQuotaDisplay();\n        return `[QUOTA] ${data.message}`;\n      }\n      return `[ERROR: ${data.error}]`;\n    }\n    // Update quota display\n    if (data.quota) {\n      state.quota = data.quota;\n      state.limits = data.limits;\n      updateQuotaDisplay();\n    }\n    return data.content || '[EMPTY]';\n  } catch (e) {\n    return `[NETWORK ERROR: ${e.message}]`;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction buildCharacterSystem(c) {\n  return `You are ${c.name}. ${c.tendencies}. Stay in character. Output a single in-character utterance (2-4 sentences) followed by a single in-character action in brackets like [climbs the boom, sniffs the salt]. Speak ONLY in character. NEVER reason out loud. NEVER explain your process.`;\n}\n\nfunction buildCharacterUser(setting, history, tickNum) {\n  const recent = history.slice(-6).map(h => {\n    if (h.turns) return h.turns.map(t => `[${t.name}]: ${(t.text || '').slice(0, 200)}`).join('\\n');\n    return `[DM]: ${(h.text || '').slice(0, 200)}`;\n  }).join('\\n\\n');\n  return `Round ${tickNum}.\n\nSetting: ${setting}\n\nPrior turns:\n${recent}\n\nYour move. Speak + action.`;\n}\n\nfunction buildDMSystem() {\n  return `You are a tight maritime-fantasy game-master. Output ONLY in-character GM narration. NEVER reason out loud. NEVER explain your process. NEVER invent cast members not given to you.`;\n}\n\nfunction buildDMOpeningPrompt(setting, cast) {\n  return `Open the night. In 3-4 sentences: who's here, what's the immediate problem, what do they need to do in the next hour. End with a question or call to action.\n\nSetting: ${setting}\n\nCast: ${cast.map(c => c.name).join(', ')}\n\nOutput ONLY prose. No preamble.`;\n}\n\nfunction buildDMClosingPrompt(recentTurns) {\n  return `What just happened:\n${recentTurns}\n\nEnd the session in 2-3 sentences: what was resolved, what carries over, what's next session's hook. End on an unresolved thread. Output ONLY the GM narration.`;\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Tick logic\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nasync function runTick() {\n  if (!state.setting.trim()) {\n    alert('Set the scene first (or click a preset).');\n    return;\n  }\n  if (state.characters.length < 2) {\n    alert('Add at least 2 characters.');\n    return;\n  }\n  const tickBtn = document.getElementById('tick-btn');\n  tickBtn.disabled = true;\n  tickBtn.textContent = '...';\n\n  state.tick++;\n  const transcriptEl = document.getElementById('transcript');\n\n  // Round 0 = DM opening\n  if (state.tick === 1 && state.transcript.length === 0) {\n    transcriptEl.innerHTML = '<div class=\"loading\">DM is opening the scene...</div>';\n    const dmOpen = await callLLM(\n      { llm: 'zai:glm-4.5' },\n      buildDMOpeningPrompt(state.setting, state.characters),\n      buildDMSystem()\n    );\n    if (dmOpen.startsWith('[ERROR')) {\n      addScar(state.tick, 'dm-error', dmOpen);\n    }\n    state.transcript.push({ tick: 1, turns: [{ name: 'DM', text: dmOpen }] });\n    render();\n    save();\n    tickBtn.disabled = false;\n    tickBtn.textContent = 'Tick \u2192';\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Subsequent rounds = all characters respond in parallel\n  transcriptEl.innerHTML = '<div class=\"loading\">All characters are responding in parallel...</div>';\n  const history = state.transcript;\n  const promises = state.characters.map(async c => {\n    const ticks = c.ticks + Math.floor(state.resonance[c.name] || 0);\n    const used = ticksUsed(c.name);\n    if (used >= ticks) {\n      return { name: c.name, text: `[off-screen \u2014 out of ticks]`, shifts: {}, shift_total: 0 };\n    }\n    try {\n      const text = await callLLM(c, buildCharacterUser(state.setting, history, state.tick), buildCharacterSystem(c));\n      const keywords = parseKeywords(c.keywords);\n      const shifts = {};\n      let total = 0;\n      const lower = (text || '').toLowerCase();\n      for (const [w, s] of Object.entries(keywords)) {\n        const cnt = (lower.match(new RegExp('\\\\b' + w + '\\\\b', 'g')) || []).length;\n        if (cnt > 0) { shifts[w] = s * cnt; total += s * cnt; }\n      }\n      return { name: c.name, text, shifts, shift_total: total };\n    } catch (e) {\n      return { name: c.name, text: `[ERROR: ${e.message}]`, shifts: {}, shift_total: 0 };\n    }\n  });\n  const turns = await Promise.all(promises);\n  const round = { tick: state.tick, turns };\n  state.transcript.push(round);\n  updateCitations(round);\n  updateResonance(round);\n  // Check for scars\n  for (const t of turns) {\n    if (t.text && t.text.startsWith('[ERROR')) {\n      addScar(state.tick, 'character-error', `${t.name} errored: ${t.text.slice(0, 100)}`);\n    }\n    if (t.text && t.text.startsWith('[off-screen')) {\n      addScar(state.tick, 'off-screen', `${t.name} ran out of ticks`);\n    }\n  }\n  render();\n  save();\n  tickBtn.disabled = false;\n  tickBtn.textContent = 'Tick \u2192';\n}\n\nasync function endScene() {\n  if (state.transcript.length === 0) return;\n  const lastRound = state.transcript[state.transcript.length - 1];\n  const recentTurns = lastRound.turns.map(t => `[${t.name}]: ${t.text}`).join('\\n\\n');\n  const closing = await callLLM(\n    { llm: 'zai:glm-4.5' },\n    buildDMClosingPrompt(recentTurns),\n    buildDMSystem()\n  );\n  state.transcript.push({ tick: state.tick, turns: [{ name: 'DM', text: closing }] });\n  render();\n  save();\n}\n\nfunction rewind() {\n  if (state.transcript.length === 0) return;\n  // Drop the last round, but add a scar\n  const lastRound = state.transcript[state.transcript.length - 1];\n  const names = (lastRound.turns || []).map(t => t.name).join(', ');\n  addScar(state.tick, 'rewind', `Dropped round ${state.tick} (${names}) \u2014 preserved as scar`);\n  state.transcript.pop();\n  state.tick = Math.max(0, state.tick - 1);\n  render();\n  save();\n}\n\nfunction addScar(tick, kind, note) {\n  // Avoid duplicate scars for the same tick\n  if (!state.scars.some(s => s.tick === tick && s.kind === kind && s.note === note)) {\n    state.scars.push({ tick, kind, note });\n  }\n}\n\nfunction resetAll() {\n  if (!confirm('Reset everything? This clears the transcript, scars, and citations.')) return;\n  state.transcript = [];\n  state.tick = 0;\n  state.citations = {};\n  state.scars = [];\n  state.resonance = {};\n  render();\n  save();\n}\n\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Wire up\n// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfunction esc(s) {\n  return String(s || '').replace(/[&<>\"']/g, c => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'})[c]);\n}\n\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n  load();\n  document.getElementById('setting').value = state.setting;\n  document.getElementById('tick-btn').onclick = runTick;\n  document.getElementById('end-btn').onclick = endScene;\n  document.getElementById('rewind-btn').onclick = rewind;\n  document.getElementById('reset-btn').onclick = resetAll;\n\n  document.querySelectorAll('.preset-btn[data-preset]').forEach(b => {\n    b.onclick = () => {\n      const key = b.dataset.preset;\n      state.characters.push(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(PRESETS[key])));\n      render();\n      save();\n    };\n  });\n  document.querySelectorAll('.preset-btn[data-setting]').forEach(b => {\n    b.onclick = () => {\n      const k = b.dataset.setting;\n      if (SETTINGS[k]) {\n        state.setting = SETTINGS[k];\n        document.getElementById('setting').value = state.setting;\n        save();\n      }\n    };\n  });\n\n  render();\n});\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}